Help for FT8 and FT4 reception

Choose the radio input in Receive Audio Setup. On Linux and Mac, YAC
selects a playback-only device when none is configured. A grid locator
is required.

Opening tunes to the selected mode’s preset on the current band and
starts decoding. If there is no preset, use e to tune and s to start.

Reviewed messages with a usable locator include an estimated distance in every filter mode.

b) Band. Tune to the selected digital mode’s receive frequency.
d) Digital Mode. Select FT8 or FT4.
e) Enter a frequency in MHz.
f) Filter decoded messages.
m) Select the radio mode.
s) Start or stop decoding.
v) Read the latest message.
w) Where am I? Read signal, frequency and mode.
Comma) Read the previous message.
Full stop) Read the next message.
c) Clear the results.
q) Stop decoding and return. The selected mode and results stay for this YAC session.

